  "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1",
  "verseCount": 18,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "1",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ECC 1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "1",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "These are the words of the Philosopher, David's son, who was king in Jerusalem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.1"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It is useless, useless, said the Philosopher. Life is useless, all useless. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You spend your life working, labouring, and what do you have to show for it? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Generations come and generations go, but the world stays just the same. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sun still rises, and it still goes down, going wearily back to where it must start all over again. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The wind blows south, the wind blows north — round and round and back again. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Every river flows into the sea, but the sea is not yet full. The water returns to where the rivers began, and starts all over again. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Everything leads to weariness — a weariness too great for words. Our eyes can never see enough to be satisfied; our ears can never hear enough. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "What has happened before will happen again. What has been done before will be done again. There is nothing new in the whole world. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Look,” they say, “here is something new!” But no, it has all happened before, long before we were born. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "No one remembers what has happened in the past, and no one in days to come will remember what happens between now and then.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.11"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I, the Philosopher, have been king over Israel in Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I determined that I would examine and study all the things that are done in this world.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "God has laid a miserable fate upon us. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I have seen everything done in this world, and I tell you, it is all useless. It is like chasing the wind. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You can't straighten out what is crooked; you can't count things that aren't there.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "1KI.4.29+1KI.4.30+1KI.4.31"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "1 Kgs 4.29–31",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I told myself, “I have become a great man, far wiser than anyone who ruled Jerusalem before me. I know what wisdom and knowledge really are.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I was determined to learn the difference between knowledge and foolishness, wisdom and madness. But I found out that I might as well be chasing the wind. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 1:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The wiser you are, the more worries you have; the more you know, the more it hurts.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.1.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.1.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
